00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.960
Stir the cheese into your pasta.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.300
мясо comes next.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.280
мясо са.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.140
мясо.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:05.840
It means meat.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.380
мясо на тарелке.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.380
That means meat is on the plate.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.420
Think my assa like my awesome sausage.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.720
Ovoch is our vegetable word.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:15.840
Ovoch.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:16.740
Ovoch.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:17.760
It means vegetable.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.120
Ovoch zеленый.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.820
That means the vegetable is grim.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:21.580
Ovoch.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.740
Sounds like a fresh vegetable from the garden.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.780
есть минсту ить.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.300
есть.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:27.880
яблоко.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.540
That means I eat an apple.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:30.480
есть.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.920
Sounds like the English word yes.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:33.660
Yes.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.640
I want to eat.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.260
пить.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.220
минсту длинг.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:36.740
пить.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:37.280
пить.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.080
молоко.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.880
That means drink milk.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:40.640
пить.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:41.560
like beat moss.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.620
but you drink instead of planting it.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:44.400
finally.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.100
вкусно.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:45.660
Вика.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.520
вкусно.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:48.800
It means delicious or tasty.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.400
это вкусно.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.820
That means this is delicious.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.460
Вика.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.220
Осна.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.240
Sounds like room.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.500
Your taste buds zoom with joy.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.600
Russian nouns have gender that change word endings.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.020
Яблоко ends in O and is neuter.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.740
Сир ends in a consonant and is masculine.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.340
молоко also ends in O and is neuter.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.920
English does not change endings for gender.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.740
We just say the red apple or the red cheese.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.040
In Russian you say вкусно яблоко.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.180
For the tasty apple.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.240
You say вкусно сыр for the tasty cheese.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.240
Now here something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.160
Want to know a secret about tea?

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.800
Did you know that the Russian word tea and the English word tea

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.620
are actually cousins from the same ancient root.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.380
They both come from the Chinese word tea.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.600
The word traveled along the Silk Road to Persian and Turkish traders.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.960
Then a rich Russian around the 17th century

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.020
when tea became popular in Moscow.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.140
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.640
But actually means shop.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.860
Next time you see tea on a menu, remember it is cousins with tea.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.540
They both come from Chinese tea.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.060
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.380
In Russia tea is more than a drink.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.700
It is a daily ritual shared with family and friends.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.920
It is often served with jam, lemon or sweets

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.220
in a special tea pod called Asamavar.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.400
Offering tea to guests is a warm sun of hospitality

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.960
that has lasted for centuries.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.040
